", "ownerFullName": "Chantel Mila", "history": [{"date": "2026-08-02", "plays": 6724, "likes": 138, "comments": 0}, {"date": "2026-08-09", "plays": 7296, "likes": 150, "comments": 0}], "still_climbing": false, "transcript": "It goes one by one, even two by two", "is_relevant": true, "hook_type": "List"}, {"shortCode": "DbSbAcASTGA", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbSbAcASTGA/", "caption": "9 of the best tips that will help you keep your food veggies fresher for longer \ud83e\udd6c\ud83c\udf45 Save this post for your next grocery shop to help avoid wastage and keep your food fresh. Which tip will you try first? Let me know what you\u2019d like to see in part 2 \ud83c\udf3b \n\n1. Berries: Store berries in a container lined with paper towel. It absorbs excess moisture, which helps slow mould growth\n2. Lettuce: Wrap lettuce in paper towel. Lettuce wilts because of moisture, so the paper towel keeps it crisp\n3. Herbs: Store herbs in a bouquet of water to keep them hydrated and prevent them drying out\n4 / 5: Avocados: Store unripe avocados at room temperature and ripe avocados in the fridge\n6. Potatoes: Store an apple with your potatoes to prevent spouting\n7. Carrots: Submerge carrots in water to keep them crunchy. This is a great one for quick lunchbox prep!\n8. Tomatoes: Store tomatoes upside down at room temperature to prevent them ripening\n9. Bananas: Wrap banana stems in foil to slow down ripening of your entire fruit bowl\n\nWhich one of your favourite? Hope these quick tips were helpful lovelies xx \n\n#fridgerestock #fridgeorganization #tipsandtricks #mamamilastips #homehacks", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:26:13.000Z", "videoDuration": 35.153, "videoPlayCount": 176733, "videoViewCount": 19399, "likesCount": -1, "commentsCount": 10, "displayUrl": "https://instagram.froo2-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t51.82787-15/757524316_18102079460190993_4515998356091266161_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_p1080x1080_sh2.08_tt6&_nc_ht=instagram.froo2-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=Q6cZ2gGzv_wR9XajHyF8AJChd6rxVn5CYQQmDlt0u0cgArV9j03O16A4wodJY-Im2tYIerE&_nc_ohc=e0ItKzDxYXYQ7kNvwH622Ie&_nc_gid=vkzRjiIqE9_zfdAqY14lzQ&edm=ADp7STQBAAAA&ccb=7-5&oh=00_AQFPToYgNukarISQ5SO7mRB_8KxgcfGNhXuEDAxzE1YMkA&oe=6A7E4915&_nc_sid=c6f216", "videoUrl": "https://instagram.froo2-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m86/AQMvmzMiyNwrPueLz47PjKW-rAbo2gWWa9wcJyQUyWlYZcjROsc648ZXZK8s8RZ1p-N8jS6hSg-UVVC2wf7K-W9YNR7V_oaA7EbXCgQ.mp4?_nc_cat=106&_nc_oc=Adr7KhtdIKXo_tHhqNRnyI-osdW7Q17xwDbW9vUq54kFDZzlhqgSpDr-DT2Tlxhj-PM&_nc_sid=5e9851&_nc_ht=instagram.froo2-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=N8AQd4X_i-AQ7kNvwHif1qV&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6Inhwdl9wcm9ncmVzc2l2ZS5JTlNUQUdSQU0uQ0xJUFMuQzMuNzIwLmRhc2hfYmFzZWxpbmVfMV92MSIsInhwdl9hc3NldF9pZCI6MTcyNzEyOTA1MTY2MjcyMSwiYXNzZXRfYWdlX2RheXMiOjEzLCJ2aV91c2VjYXNlX2lkIjoxMDA5OSwiZHVyYXRpb25fcyI6MzUsInVybGdlbl9zb3VyY2UiOiJ3d3cifQ%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&vs=40059dc7158e2f0f&_nc_&_nc_gid=vkzRjiIqE9_zfdAqY14lzQ&_nc_ss=7a22e&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQGzdPJc0WKo9MWFMpENEaozLEFHS3z-rML-5PJM9-t0kw&oe=6A7A36FF", "musicInfo": {"artist_name": "mama_mila_au", "song_name": "Original audio", "uses_original_audio": true, "should_mute_audio": false, "should_mute_audio_reason": "", "audio_id": "27986753934254737"}, "ownerUsername": "mama_mila_au", "ownerFullName": "Chantel Mila", "history": [{"date": "2026-08-02", "plays": 162899, "likes": -1, "comments": 9}, {"date": "2026-08-09", "plays": 176733, "likes": -1, "comments": 10}], "still_climbing": false, "transcript": "If your fruit and veggies seem to go bad the minute you buy them, here are nine storage hacks to help keep them fresher for longer. Store berries in a container lined with a paper towel that absorbs excess moisture, which helps slow mould growth. Wrap lettuce in a paper towel. Lettuce wilts because of moisture, so the paper towel helps keep it crisp. Store herbs in a bouquet of water to keep them hydrated and prevent them drying out. Store unripe avocados at room temperature and ripe avocados in the fridge. And this one's my favourite. Store an apple with your potatoes to prevent spouting. Submerge carrots in water to keep them crunchy. And store tomatoes upside down at room temperature. And wrap the stems of your bananas in foil to slow down ripening.", "is_relevant": false}, {"shortCode": "DbFzHjySc7y", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbFzHjySc7y/", "caption": "Which trick will you try first? Follow along for more daily home tips + let me know your requests in the comments xx \n\n#hometips #homehacks #cleaninghacks #cleaningtips", "timestamp": "2026-07-22T09:46:52.000Z", "videoDuration": 21.933, "videoPlayCount": 106850, "videoViewCount": 14767, "likesCount": 4055, "commentsCount": 7, "displayUrl": "https://scontent-nrt1-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/753748014_18101573462190993_2947788658586313333_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_p1080x1080_sh2.08_tt6&_nc_ht=scontent-nrt1-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=Q6cZ2gGC4xKVWmkoLs7P9jOMoXRqxxjuTvl9L3yUn-IkuT0DsMMQjMvM9DHuZ5wTYyCsJlc&_nc_ohc=NFE_D23pDUsQ7kNvwFq3AjI&_nc_gid=fVRy1c_H1y5hTWx_i98ddA&edm=ADp7STQBAAAA&ccb=7-5&oh=00_AQErjT7nVsoSYZ2aM5dRnub6FHntI0-hkhmlxRMxxdgQ8Q&oe=6A7E2C7C&_nc_sid=c6f216", "videoUrl": "https://scontent-nrt6-1.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t2/f2/m367/AQO5H74xkG02geLQ2WHKbr9lzNTPInW8_mEwrEbBxXO_OiHSTTuwKvxiUkle9Pwfy98zkAJUvVE4Q2hPOvoO34bdjyEGrxXbSdlyrJI.mp4?_nc_cat=111&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=scontent-nrt6-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_ohc=UODTqlnmjEcQ7kNvwGr2gRn&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=fVRy1c_H1y5hTWx_i98ddA&_nc_zt=28&_nc_ss=7a22e&oh=00_AQGCb-L1tzuMWH7mlZXb5kXDqFoL_4BlxYbMzEGL1mvhfw&oe=6A7E2F20", "musicInfo": {"artist_name": "mama_mila_au", "song_name": "Original audio", "uses_original_audio": true, "should_mute_audio": false, "should_mute_audio_reason": "", "audio_id": "28135660782698213"}, "ownerUsername": "mama_mila_au", "ownerFullName": "Chantel Mila", "history": [{"date": "2026-07-26", "plays": 66262, "likes": 2868, "comments": 5}, {"date": "2026-08-02", "plays": 88956, "likes": 3654, "comments": 6}, {"date": "2026-08-09", "plays": 106850, "likes": 4055, "comments": 7}], "still_climbing": false, "transcript": "Life hacks to keep bugs and spiders away from your home. Place peppermint oil on cotton balls and put them under your bin liner to repel bugs, and you can also place these in your vacuum to make your home smell like peppermint. Repel ants from your home using rosemary-infused water. Pour boiling water down your drains to keep fruit flies away, and spiders hate citrus, so wipe down your walls and floors with citrus oil or citrus peels.", "is_relevant": true, "hook_type": "List"}, {"shortCode": "DbFpYC9p5j8", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbFpYC9p5j8/", "caption": "Which trick will you try first? \ud83c\udf3b save this video to bring that hotel feeling home x \n1. Start with your mattress, remove stains instantly using shaving cream \n2. Then vacuum your mattress to rid dust mites and odours\n3. Mix 1 cup water, 1 tbs rubbing alcohol and vanilla oil to clean dust from your bedsides (leave out the essential oil if you have pets!)\n4. And you can use this mix as a linen spray for ongoing fragrance \n5. And you guys know how much I love to heat lemon, rosemary, clove and vanilla to make your room smell incredible \n\nWhich one is your favourite? Hope these were helpful lovelies xx \n\n#bedroommakeover #homefragrance #hometips #homehacks #tipsandtricks", "timestamp": "2026-07-22T08:22:31.000Z", "videoDuration": 23.6, "videoPlayCount": 358363, "videoViewCount": 21964, "likesCount": 6320, "commentsCount": 43, "displayUrl": "https://scontent-lhr6-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/755264137_18101650634190993_7746453329349717573_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_p1080x1080_sh2.08_tt6&_nc_ht=scontent-lhr6-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=Q6cZ2gFmRAjg1gifA8HzG2Vk-wsToXPU9pbXQlRDB1UCzEzAJ_wNTArsRhveva8HlPq2MjA&_nc_ohc=GqeyJgy-TPoQ7kNvwGGKfLq&_nc_gid=HiLMshrkRIMpqBmbPflahg&edm=ADp7STQBAAAA&ccb=7-5&oh=00_AQF7nvungKkAu4X7tuc2grG1xspYGJP7VKLIkMyiqn8WTw&oe=6A7E442D&_nc_sid=c6f216", "videoUrl": "https://scontent-lhr11